<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n82907" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πηδόν</span></b> , τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>blade of an oar</i>: hence
			generally, <i>oar</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀναρρίπτειν ἅλα πηδῷ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					7.328
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				13.78
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πηδοῖσιν ἐρέσσετε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					4.200
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γῆ δὲ ναυσθλωθήσεται ῥήσσοντι πηδοῖς
					χέρσον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lyc.
					1416
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in pl.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πηδά,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πηδάλια</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Arat.
				155
			</span></i>. (Written <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πῆδον</span>, also
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πῆδος</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
